{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383790-do-you-base-your-character-on-yourself","id":1383790,"title":"Do you base your character on yourself?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-25T10:18:50-07:00","id":1383790,"title":"Do you base your character on yourself?","content":"I was thinking about the do vampires have sex question in another thread. <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'd guess it matters more to players than story tellers who are trying to identify with their character. I would guess most people invested in just one character for years have a bigger issue with thinking themselves impotent especially if they are basing the character on themselves. Maybe I'm off base, but it leads me to this topic.<br /> <br /> As a player I based most of my characters on whatever role I was making them for but some times I would make an awesome version of myself. I'd give him skills and stats I felt reflected an idealized version of myself. Anyone else?</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:46:23-07:00","id":1383795,"title":"","content":"I think it really depends on the player and the game style you are playing.<br /> <br /> For instance I have STed games where a player couldn't wrap their minds around a character unless it was very similar to themselves, while another player in the same group refused to player a character unless it was as different as possible from themselves.<br /> <br /> Alternatively if you are just flat out playing a &quot;play as yourself&quot; game, that makes things even more confusing.<br /> <br /> When it comes to being invested in a character it really comes down to why you are playing the character. For some people the character is a therapeutic outlet where they can rage or behave transgressively with few if any repercussions. For other people the character is inspired by an outside source and they just want to explore the concept and its ramifications.<br /> <br /> The one thing I have noticed is if the player has IRL knowledge that is part of the character, then they automatically &quot;sink into character&quot; faster and more smoothly, which in turn helps the rest of the group do the same. So the investment isn't always being a reflection of the self as much as a point of automatic similarity by virtue of shared expertise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:47:50-07:00","id":1383796,"title":"","content":"Absolutely not. Though I do find most of my characters end up calculating and paranoid unless I specifically try to avoid it. I play very different characters, I enjoy exploring other people who are very different from myself, and I'm comfortable with them doing things I wouldn't be comfortable doing in real life or having ideologies I absolutely don't agree with. If my characters represented a better version of me, I'd be locked up for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-25-2020, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T11:02:21-07:00","id":1383800,"title":"","content":"Yes, I am incredibly sexy and rich.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T12:12:08-07:00","id":1383814,"title":"","content":"I made a Vampire once where I spent points in a way to reflect my strengths and reading the skill descriptions &quot;ok 2 points in drive stick shift no problem&quot; etc... lotta 1's and 2's. I don't know if I could trust my friends not to kill me, I think I may have been offended if they had wacked a vampire with my name. It was interesting to see where the starter vampire points spread out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T13:20:39-07:00","id":1383830,"title":"","content":"No, I mostly base my characters on a blend of archetypes from fiction, and the tenants of various paths. Like even if I'm playing a character on humanity, or in a game with no morality stat, I'll often base my behaviors on modified versions of the paths like Honorable Accord, Feral Heart, and Power and Inner Voice. I find the Paths/Roads really useful when I'm struggling to think of what my character's in-character reaction to something should be. I'll keep a tab open to whichever path I've picked so I can give it a quick glance when I'm playing in Roll 20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T14:27:18-07:00","id":1383844,"title":"","content":"I don't consciously base pcs on myself. After playing a few sessions, though, I always seem to find there is some commonality between me and my characters. Similar communication styles, or coping mechanisms for stress, for example.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if that's inherent to the creative process, or if I have a habit of looking for the things I share in common with fictional characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T15:01:29-07:00","id":1383849,"title":"","content":"I feel uncomfortable with low-humanity characters, and my characters tend to have a very analytical way of thinking. To that extent yes.<br /> <br /> However, a character whose idea of a good time is to sit alone in a library reading a good book would not work in a game context, My characters have a social and adventurous side which is the antithesis of who I am. (Though come to think of it, my favourite clans, the Gangrel and Nosferatu, are not noted for their sociability). I'd say they aren't so much an idealized version of me as an alternate one, liking things I'd never like, enjoying experiences I'd never enjoy. Manifestations of the road not taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T15:30:07-07:00","id":1383853,"title":"","content":"I try not to, but inevitably, yourself tends to come through in every character you play to a degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T15:32:57-07:00","id":1383854,"title":"","content":"I usually base characters on myself (or at least try to),<br /> it's mostly because I'm lazy and not very good at copying characters from movies/books<br /> <br /> it can get really depressing though, especially if your character has plot armour and survives despite all their flaws, and you get to not only endure such flaws but witness their effects on your surroundings (a surrounding that doesn't have the privilege of plot armour)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T07:15:11-07:00","id":1383951,"title":"","content":"I ST a lot, all of my controlled characters have small a piece of me, since I am interpreting them; however if it is an existing character from the lore, I tend to use whatever knowledge I have from descriptions, novels or any other source.<br /> <br /> When I want to make new background characters I tend to copy from Babylon 5 (for speech / mannerisms), 24 (pragmatical behaviour), and people I know. I tend to give them detailed merits and flaws, whether plot relevant or randomly selected, end up very realistic IMHO. My players have spoken highly of my characterisations, but truly most of it comes from selected media or the real world itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-26-2020, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T09:41:51-07:00","id":1383966,"title":"","content":"My favorite metaphor about character creation is that the characters you make are <i>alternate </i>versions of yourself. They are a chance for you to explore what you would be like under different circumstances, a chance to explore different aspects of your personality. And even if you try to deliberately differentiate your characters from yourself, you're still probably going to draw on people you've encountered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T11:22:14-07:00","id":1383979,"title":"","content":"Usually, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T12:00:30-07:00","id":1383985,"title":"","content":"No, and when I'm ST'ing I try to encourage players (especially newer ones) not to make characters that are too similar or too heavily based on themselves either. Over the years I've found that it makes it a little too easy for a player to identify their character if the character is based off of them, and if there's any kind of issues or problems with that character, they are much more likely to take that as criticism personally by seeing it as criticism of him or herself rather than the character. And having a player or the ST start criticizing <i>another player</i> (or at least having that criticized player feel the criticism is directed at them rather than at a character) is a great way to end up with serious drama and groups imploding.<br /> <br /> So while having a character similar to you can make roleplaying a bit easier, as an ST I just find it presents a few potential big problems that I'd just as soon try to head off.<br /> <br /> That's not to say I've never run games like that before. One time I ran a short 3 shot game where I had the players make characters based on themselves (even the same name and everything) and then.... bam, they all got gunned down in a shopping mall 10 minutes into the first session and then woke up in the Shadowlands as Wraiths. Made for a fun way to introduce the group to Wraith, but it was more like a one time gimmick than something I'd encourage players to do more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T21:29:41-07:00","id":1384101,"title":"","content":"Not in general. The whole point of a role playing game is to get to play characters who think and do things differently from yourself; a come-as-you-aren't party, as it were. I have found it advantageous to set a character's intelligence in the same ballpark as my own, though. It's really frustrating to bite my tongue and pretend not to notice or understand things that my character wouldn't. And a game where a plainspoken, somewhat dim acquaintance played a polymath genius was cringeworthy enough that I consider myself well warned against playing a genius myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}